From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a touchpad pinch always zooms the desk

A two-finger pinch went to the page or native app under the pointer
first, as a synthetic ctrl+wheel, and zoomed the desk only when that
window left it alone. Over a native app it never did. The pinch now
always zooms the desk, the outermost page, like a magnifier, whatever
window is under the pointer (user, 2026-11-09).

- `RenderWidgetHostInputEventRouter::RouteTouchpadGestureEvent` hands
  a touchpad pinch's begin, updates and end straight to the root view,
  without the wheel step, so no hit test runs and no page or `<app>`
  can claim it. It reaches the root's page scale as an unconsumed
  pinch would have.
- Pinches the shell binds, of three or four fingers, never get here:
  the platform hands them to `DeskGestures` first.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 .../input/render_widget_host_input_event_router.cc  | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/components/input/render_widget_host_input_event_router.cc b/components/input/render_widget_host_input_event_router.cc
index c8e5f07..f545978 100644
--- a/components/input/render_widget_host_input_event_router.cc
+++ b/components/input/render_widget_host_input_event_router.cc
@@ -1967,6 +1967,19 @@ void RenderWidgetHostInputEventRouter::RouteTouchpadGestureEvent(
     const blink::WebGestureEvent* event,
     const ui::LatencyInfo& latency) {
   DCHECK_EQ(blink::WebGestureDevice::kTouchpad, event->SourceDevice());
+  // domicile: a touchpad pinch always zooms the desk, the outermost page, as
+  // a magnifier, whatever window is under the pointer. No page or native app
+  // sees it: it skips hit testing and the synthetic ctrl+wheel that would let
+  // one claim it, and goes straight to the root's page scale.
+  if (event->GetType() == blink::WebInputEvent::Type::kGesturePinchBegin ||
+      event->GetType() == blink::WebInputEvent::Type::kGesturePinchUpdate ||
+      event->GetType() == blink::WebInputEvent::Type::kGesturePinchEnd) {
+    blink::WebGestureEvent pinch(*event);
+    pinch.SetNeedsWheelEvent(false);
+    pinch.has_native_pinch = false;
+    root_view->ProcessGestureEvent(pinch, latency);
+    return;
+  }
   event_targeter_->FindTargetAndDispatch(root_view, *event, latency);
 }
 
